THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-21, part 3) — federate the CRM to the tenant's Keycloak
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: a Keycloak (OIDC) provider for Relaticle's Socialite seam and the two
public routes that drive a federated sign-in, so the CRM accepts the SAME
identity that signs the brand into the platform console — the tenant's own
Keycloak realm `tenant-<slug>` — instead of a brokered stored credential.

Reason: the previous session broker minted a one-time Relaticle login from a
platform-held identity. The operator decision (2026-10-20) is to FEDERATE each
module to Keycloak OIDC rather than broker a session, so this replaces the CRM
half with a real Authorization Code + PKCE round trip against the tenant's realm.
Relaticle is one deployment serving every tenant, so the realm is not a
deployment-wide `config/services.php` client: it is named per request
(`{workspace}` whose slug is the realm suffix), which is what makes the
federation per-tenant rather than one shared login.

Files added:
  app/Socialite/KeycloakProvider.php
      a bespoke Socialite provider (public client + PKCE; internal base URL for
      the server-side token/userinfo calls, public origin for the browser hop)
  app/Http/Controllers/Platform/KeycloakFederationController.php
      start: GET /auth/keycloak/{workspace}  — begin the tenant's OIDC round trip
      callback: GET /auth/keycloak/callback  — redeem the code, land in the panel

Files modified:
  routes/web.php        registers /auth/keycloak/{workspace} and
                        /auth/keycloak/callback, NOT under `guest`/`auth`: a
                        stale session from another tenant must still be switched
                        to the workspace the console named
  config/services.php   a `keycloak` block holding DEPLOYMENT-WIDE values only
                        (public client id, the internal base URL, and an optional
                        public origin override). The realm is per-tenant and
                        never appears in config.

NO UPSTREAM LOGIC WAS ALTERED. The Socialite callback Relaticle already ships is
left in place and untouched; this is a separate provider plus two new routes.


THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-23, part 4) — tenant surface: no workspace creation, the
tenant's own name on the chrome
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: one predicate — "did this session arrive through the platform's federated
hand-off?" — and the two rules that follow from it.

Reason: the platform creates each tenant's workspace itself, so a tenant that
could create another one would sit outside the orchestrator's tenant list while
looking connected (nothing provisions, bills or tears that workspace down). The
CRM also rendered its own product mark on a surface that belongs to the reseller
and the tenant, not to us.

WHAT MARKS A TENANT SESSION: the federated identity link
`UserSocialAccount(provider_name: 'keycloak', provider_id: '<realm>|<sub>')` whose
realm is `tenant-<slug>` — written only by the federation callback above. A local
user (upstream's own self-host onboarding) has no such link, so it keeps the
registration flow and the deployment's own name; that is what keeps this fork
cheap to rebase.

