THE MODIFICATION (2026-10-23, part 5) — server-side sign-out and RP-initiated logout
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Added: a route that ends THIS session server-side (deleting its `sessions` row,
not just the browser's cookie), RP-initiated logout against the tenant realm's
`end_session_endpoint`, and the closure of the CRM's own login surface when the
deployment declares a platform console.

Reason: the console's sign-out could only clear cookies. Relaticle keeps its
session in the `sessions` table (SESSION_DRIVER=database), so a copied or replayed
cookie stayed a live tenant after "sign out" — the platform contract (§3.3) calls
that clearing, not revocation. Upstream's own revoke is a CSRF-guarded POST on a
rendered form, which a sign-out that has already navigated away cannot post; and a
tenant must not meet a second, unmanaged password form at `/crm/login` (§8 item 3).

Files added:
  app/Http/Controllers/Platform/LogoutController.php
      GET /auth/logout: auth()->logout() -> session()->invalidate() ->
      session()->regenerateToken() (the same trio as upstream's
      Filament\Auth\Http\Controllers\LogoutController), then JSON
      {revoked, end_session_url}, or a 302 to the realm end-session URL with
      ?continue=1. NOT under `auth`/`guest`: an already-dead session is a 200
      {"revoked": false} no-op, because the caller cannot follow a redirect.
  app/Support/Platform/KeycloakEndSession.php
      builds <origin>/realms/<realm>/protocol/openid-connect/logout with
      id_token_hint + client_id + post_logout_redirect_uri; holds the session key
      the callback writes and the sign-out reads.
